{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9115-1","published":"2026-11-17T00:51:50Z","modified":"2026-11-18T00:58:39.423999874Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2016-4570","UBUNTU-CVE-2016-4571","UBUNTU-CVE-2018-20004"],"upstream":["CVE-2016-4570","CVE-2016-4571","CVE-2018-20004","UBUNTU-CVE-2016-4570","UBUNTU-CVE-2016-4571","UBUNTU-CVE-2018-20004"],"summary":"mxml vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that Mini-XML used unbounded recursion when deleting and\nwriting XML nodes. An attacker could possibly use these issues to cause\nMini-XML to crash, resulting in a denial of service. These issues only\naffected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-4570, CVE-2016-4571)\n\nIt was discovered that Mini-XML incorrectly handled certain floating point\nvalues when writing XML nodes, leading to a stack-based buffer overflow. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause Mini-XML to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2018-20004)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"mxml","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/mxml?arch=source&distro=esm-apps-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.9-0ubuntu2+esm1"}]}],"versions":["2.7-1","2.9-0ubuntu1","2.9-0ubuntu2"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"libmxml1","binary_version":"2.9-0ubuntu2+esm1"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"CVE-2016-4570","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2016-4571","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2018-20004","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]}],"ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS"},"source":"https://github.com/